							"@type": "Question",
							"name": "How is bus fare computed in Metro Manila?",
							"acceptedAnswer": {
								"@type": "Answer",
								"text": "City buses (PUB) use a 5-kilometer base distance. Under the September 28, 2026 LTFRB fare guide, regular ordinary (non-aircon) city buses charge ₱15.00 for the first 5 km plus ₱2.49 for every succeeding kilometer (₱12.00 discounted base). Air-conditioned city buses charge ₱18.00 for the first 5 km plus ₱2.98 for every succeeding kilometer (₱14.40 / ₱14.50 rounded discounted base)."
							}
						},
