							"@type": "Question",
							"name": "What is the fare difference between Modern Jeepneys and Traditional Jeepneys?",
							"acceptedAnswer": {
								"@type": "Answer",
								"text": "Under official LTFRB guidelines, Modern Jeepneys (MPUJ) charge ₱17.00 for the first 4 km and ₱2.40 for each succeeding kilometer (₱13.60 discounted base + ₱1.92/km). Traditional Jeepneys (TPUJ) charge ₱14.00 for the first 4 km and ₱2.00 for each succeeding kilometer (₱11.20 discounted base + ₱1.60/km). Modern jeepneys carry a higher tariff because they are equipped with air conditioning, Euro-4 or electric powertrains, CCTV monitoring, and GPS tracking."
							}
						},
						{
							"@type": "Question",
							"name": "Can jeepney and bus drivers refuse large bills like ₱500 or ₱1,000?",
							"acceptedAnswer": {
								"@type": "Answer",
								"text": "Philippine currency notes are legal tender, but the LTFRB advises commuters to pay with reasonable denominations (₱20, ₱50, or ₱100 bills and coins) suited to their fare amount. Drivers and conductors are not permitted to refuse passenger carriage, but paying with ₱500 or ₱1,000 for a ₱14.00 minimum fare can cause significant delays during morning trips when driver coin boxes have minimal change."
							}
						},
						{
							"@type": "Question",
