		<!-- COMPREHENSIVE EDITORIAL ARTICLE (phtools.me Style) -->
		<article class="prose prose-stone max-w-4xl mx-auto font-serif text-mapa-ink pt-6 border-t border-mapa-contour/60">
			<!-- Article Header -->
			<div class="mb-10">
				<span class="font-sans text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-mapa-green">
					Commuter Guide & Consumer Rights
				</span>
				<h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-mapa-green font-serif tracking-tight mt-2">
					How Philippine Public Transit Fares Work: Rules, Formulas & Discounts
				</h2>
				<p class="font-sans text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/70 mt-2 leading-relaxed">
					Understanding the official LTFRB fare formula, why modern jeepneys cost more than traditional ones, your rights to a 20% discount on weekends under RA 11314, and what to do if an operator overcharges you.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Section 1: The Piecewise Math -->
			<section class="mb-10 font-sans">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-4">
					1. The Piecewise Math of Philippine Transit Fares
				</h3>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Every franchised Public Utility Vehicle (PUV) operating in the Philippines operates under tariff rates established by the <strong>Land Transportation Franchising and Regulatory Board (LTFRB)</strong> pursuant to the <strong>Public Service Act (Commonwealth Act No. 146)</strong>.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Unlike ride-hailing applications that use dynamic surge pricing algorithms, all public buses and jeepneys use a strict <strong>piecewise linear distance formula</strong>:
				</p>

				<div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm my-6 space-y-2">
					<div class="text-mapa-clay font-sans text-xs uppercase font-bold mb-1">Standard Statutory Distance Formula:</div>
					<div class="text-mapa-green font-bold">If Distance ≤ Base Distance (4 or 5 km):</div>
					<div class="pl-4">Legal Fare = Base Fare</div>
					<div class="text-mapa-green font-bold mt-2">If Distance > Base Distance:</div>
					<div class="pl-4">Legal Fare = Base Fare + [(Distance - Base Distance) × Succeeding Per-KM Rate]</div>
				</div>

				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed">
					For example, under the September 28, 2026 LTFRB Fare Guide, if you board a Traditional Jeepney for a <strong>10-kilometer</strong> commute, the first 4 kilometers cost <strong>PHP 14.00</strong>. The remaining 6 kilometers are charged at <strong>PHP 2.00 per kilometer</strong> (6 &times; PHP 2.00 = PHP 12.00). The total legal fare is <strong>PHP 26.00</strong> (or <strong>PHP 20.75</strong> with the 20% Student/Senior/PWD discount, rounded to the nearest 25 centavos).
				</p>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 2: Traditional vs Modern Jeepneys -->
			<section class="mb-10 font-sans border-t border-mapa-contour/40 pt-8">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-4">
					2. Traditional Jeepneys vs Modern E-Jeepneys: Why the Price Difference?
				</h3>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Under the DOTr Public Utility Vehicle Modernization Program (PUVMP) and Department Order No. 2017-011, Modern Public Utility Jeepneys (MPUJs) are classified as a higher-tier service category than traditional iconic jeepneys.
				</p>
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 my-4">
					<div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/80">
						<h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-mapa-rust mb-2">Modern PUJs (Class 2 & Class 3)</h4>
						<ul class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 space-y-1.5 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-4">
							<li>Base Fare: <strong>PHP 17.00</strong> (first 4 km) + <strong>PHP 2.40/km</strong> (Discounted: PHP 13.60 base + PHP 1.92/km).</li>
							<li>Air-conditioned cabins, Euro-4 compliant or electric motors.</li>
							<li>Equipped with CCTV cameras, GPS tracking units, and automatic fare collection (AFCS) Beep readers.</li>
							<li>Higher capital acquisition cost (PHP 2.4M to PHP 2.8M per minibus) amortized by transport cooperatives.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>

					<div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/80">
						<h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-mapa-green mb-2">Traditional PUJs</h4>
						<ul class="text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 space-y-1.5 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-4">
							<li>Base Fare: <strong>PHP 14.00</strong> (first 4 km) + <strong>PHP 2.00/km</strong> (Discounted: PHP 11.20 base + PHP 1.60/km).</li>
							<li>Open-air non-airconditioned chassis with parallel bench seating.</li>
							<li>Operated by individual single-unit operators or local transport associations.</li>
							<li>Lower operational baseline reflecting historical tariff benchmarks.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 3: Rail Transit Tariff Mechanics -->
			<section class="mb-10 font-sans border-t border-mapa-contour/40 pt-8">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-4">
					3. Rail Transit Tariff Structures: LRT-1, LRT-2, and MRT-3
				</h3>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Metro Manila's rapid transit network uses a hybrid distance tariff regulated by the Rail Regulatory Unit of the Department of Transportation, with a special <strong>50% discount for Students, Senior Citizens, and PWDs</strong> across all three lines:
				</p>
				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-xs">
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/70">
						<div class="font-bold text-sm text-mapa-green mb-1">LRT Line 1 (Green Line)</div>
						<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
							Operated by Light Rail Manila Corporation (LRMC). Boarding fee: PHP 16.25 + PHP 1.47 per kilometer (effective April 2, 2025). End-to-end trip from Fernando Poe Jr. (Roosevelt) to Dr. Santos in Parañaque (25 stations) costs PHP 52 on Stored Value Cards (PHP 55 Single Journey Ticket).
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/70">
						<div class="font-bold text-sm text-mapa-navy mb-1">LRT Line 2 (Purple Line)</div>
						<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
							Operated by Light Rail Transit Authority (LRTA). Boarding fee: PHP 13.29 + PHP 1.21 per kilometer. Full transit from Recto in Manila to Antipolo in Rizal (13 stations) costs PHP 14 to PHP 33 on Stored Value Cards (PHP 15 to PHP 35 Single Journey Ticket).
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour/70">
						<div class="font-bold text-sm text-mapa-rust mb-1">MRT Line 3 (Blue Line)</div>
						<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
							Operated by DOTr MRT-3 Project Management Office. Station-to-station matrix tiers: PHP 13, PHP 16, PHP 20, PHP 24, and PHP 28. Complete end-to-end trip from North Avenue to Taft Avenue (13 stations, 16.9 km) is capped at PHP 28.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 4: Student & Senior Rights -->
			<section class="mb-10 font-sans border-t border-mapa-contour/40 pt-8">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-4">
					4. Your 20% Discount Rights Under Philippine Republic Acts
				</h3>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					The 20% passenger fare discount is not an optional courtesy granted by drivers. It is a <strong>mandatory statutory right</strong> enacted by Congress through multiple national laws:
				</p>

				<div class="space-y-4 my-6">
					<div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border-l-4 border-mapa-green border-y border-r border-mapa-contour/80">
						<h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-mapa-green mb-1">
							Republic Act No. 11314 (Student Fare Discount Act)
						</h4>
						<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
							Covers all Filipino students from elementary through college, technical-vocational, and post-secondary institutions. <strong>Crucially, RA 11314 grants the discount 365 days a year: including weekends, summer breaks, semestral vacations, and national holidays.</strong> Drivers who refuse the discount on a Sunday or holiday are directly violating national law.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border-l-4 border-mapa-flag-blue border-y border-r border-mapa-contour/80">
						<h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-mapa-flag-blue mb-1">
							Republic Act No. 9994 (Expanded Senior Citizens Act)
						</h4>
						<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
							Grants Filipino resident citizens aged 60 and above a 20% discount on all public land transit (jeepneys, buses, trains, and taxis) upon presentation of an OSCA ID, senior citizen card, or valid government passport or driver's license showing date of birth.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border-l-4 border-mapa-rust border-y border-r border-mapa-contour/80">
						<h4 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-mapa-rust mb-1">
							Republic Act No. 9442 & RA 10754 (Magna Carta for Persons with Disabilities)
						</h4>
						<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-mapa-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
							Guarantees a 20% discount and VAT exemption on domestic land, sea, and air transit upon presentation of a valid PWD ID issued by the National Council on Disability Affairs (NCDA) or municipal Persons with Disability Affairs Office (PDAO).
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 5: What to Do If Overcharged -->
			<section class="mb-10 font-sans border-t border-mapa-contour/40 pt-8">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-4">
					5. What to Do If You Are Overcharged or Denied a Discount
				</h3>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Every franchised PUV driver is legally required to post an official laminated copy of the <strong>LTFRB Fare Matrix (*Talaan ng Pamasahe*)</strong> inside the vehicle. If a driver cannot produce or display the matrix, they are barred from collecting rate increases under LTFRB Memorandum Circular No. 2019-035.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-mapa-ink/90 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Under Joint Administrative Order (JAO) No. 2014-01, public utility drivers who overcharge passengers or refuse legally mandated discounts face heavy statutory penalties:
				</p>
				<ul class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-mapa-ink/85 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-5 mb-4">
					<li><strong>First Offense:</strong> PHP 5,000 fine</li>
					<li><strong>Second Offense:</strong> PHP 10,000 fine and vehicle impoundment for 30 days</li>
					<li><strong>Third & Subsequent Offenses:</strong> PHP 15,000 fine and cancellation of Certificate of Public Convenience (CPC)</li>
				</ul>
				<div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour space-y-3 text-xs sm:text-sm">
					<div class="font-bold text-mapa-green font-serif text-base mb-1">Step-by-Step Overcharging Complaint Procedure:</div>
					<div>1. <strong>Take note of critical identifiers:</strong> The vehicle's license plate number (e.g. ABC 1234), body number, franchise cooperative name, and exact route name.</div>
					<div>2. <strong>Record transaction details:</strong> Note the date, exact time, boarding location, and alighting destination.</div>
					<div>3. <strong>File an official report:</strong>
						<ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-1.5 space-y-1 text-mapa-ink/80">
							<li><strong>LTFRB 24/7 Hotline:</strong> Dial <strong>1342</strong></li>
							<li><strong>LTFRB Viber Complaint Line:</strong> <strong>0928-886-4244</strong></li>
							<li><strong>Official Email:</strong> <code>complaints@ltfrb.gov.ph</code></li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Section 6: Official Citations -->
			<section class="mb-10 font-sans border-t border-mapa-contour/40 pt-8">
				<h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-4">
					6. Official Citations & Legal Framework
				</h3>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed">
